From c81e8862923c5964f43e86050b0f1907397dd50d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:03:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] glib: Render dynamic XFA forms

poppler_document_render_xfa() runs the XFA form of a document and returns
a document with the generated pages and AcroForm fields. Changes made
through those fields are passed to the form, and
poppler_document_xfa_needs_rerender() tells when its scripts changed the
form so that the document should be rendered again. Messages, URLs and
print requests of the scripts are available through
poppler_document_xfa_take_messages(), _take_urls() and
_take_print_request(). Printing uses a variant of the pages without the
objects that are relevant on screen only.

Setting the state of a push button of a rendered form clicks it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
